Backport of upstream i386 decoder / segment fixes that era code trips:
  380b95961817 (2026-06-21) decode opcode extensions group 3 /1 as TEST
    (F6 /1 and F7 /1 are an undocumented TEST alias; packers use it)
  e38d0afade7c (2026-05-28) apply mod to immediate count of an RCL/RCR
    operation (8/16-bit counts are reduced modulo 9/17, immediates too)
  36f634fe4ab6 (2026-06-22) allow transition to virtual-8086 mode only if
    CPL == 0 and CPU is not in long mode (IRET/task switch into V86)
  106d766c9d5b (2025-11-15) fix stack size when delivering real mode
    interrupts (SS size honoured instead of always 16-bit)
  0d22b621b796 (2025-10-13) fix access to the T bit of the TSS
  ebb46ba6a4a2 (2025-11-14) validate segment registers (mov to a segment
    register 6/7 or to CS is #UD, was silently accepted)
  4f503afc7eb5 (2025-10-21) Correctly handle invalid 0x0f 0xc7 0xxx insns
Hunk 1 of e38d0afade7c re-applied by hand (context only). Not taken:
60efba3c1bff (user-mode only), the MOVBE/CRC32/VEX fixes (a Pentium 3
never decodes them). Drop when the base moves past QEMU 11.1.

